k whether the filament is stuck in the tool head.␀AMS-HT H has detected a breakage of the PTFE tube during filament loading. Please check whether the PTFE tubes inside and outside the AMS have fallen off or been damaged.␀AMS-HT H feed-out Hall sensor is disconnected. The connector may have poor contact.␀AMS-HT H feed-in Hall sensor is disconnected, which may be due to poor connector contact.␀Failed to extrude AMS-HT H filament; the extruder may be clogged or the filament may be too thin, causing the extruder to slip.␀AMS-HT H feeds filament out of AMS timeout.␀AMS-HT H pulls filament back to AMS timeout.␀AMS-HT H feeder unit motor is stalled, cannot rotate the spool.␀AMS-HT H feeder unit motor has no signal, which may be due to poor contact in the motor connector or a motor fault.␀AMS-HT H filament odometer has no signal, which may be due to poor contact in the odometer connector or a odometer fault.␀AMS-HT H filament status is abnormal, which may be due to a filament breakage inside the AMS.␀AMS-HT H assist motor has slipped. Please pull out the filament, cut off the worn part, and then try again.␀AMS-HT H assist motor is stalled, due to excessive resistance in the tube between AMS and the printer.␀AMS-HT H assist motor is stalled, due to excessive resistance in the tube near AMS.␀AMS-HT H assist motor is stalled, due to excessive resistance in the tube between AMS and the filament buffer.␀AMS-HT H assist motor is stalled, due to excessive resistance in the tube near the filament buffer.␀AMS-HT H assist motor is stalled, due to excessive resistance in the tube between the filament buffer and the toolhead.␀AMS-HT H assist motor is stalled, due to excessive resistance in the tube near the toolhead.␀The tube inside the AMS-HT H is broken, or feed-out hall sensor is faulty and cannot detect the filament.␀AMS-HT H failed to rotate the filament spool when pulling filament back to AMS.␀AMS-HT H feed resistance is too high. Please reduce spool rotation resistance and avoid over-bent or over-long filament tubes.␀AMS-HT H filament has run out. Please wait while old filament is purged.␀AMS-HT H filament has run out and automatically switched to the slot with the same filament.␀AMS-HT H door detection is abnormal, the Hall sensor connection may be loose or disconnected.␀AMS-HT H front cover is open. This may affect the drying performance or cause the filament to absorb moisture.␀AMS-HT H uses printer power for drying during loading/printing. For better drying performance, please connect a power adapter.␀The AMS-HT H RFID 1 board has an error.␀The RFID-tag on AMS-HT H is damaged, or its content cannot be identified.␀The AMS-HT H RFID 2 board has an error.␀AMS-HT H The humidity sensor is disconnected, which may be due to poor connector contact.␀AMS-HT H Filament buffer position signal lost: the cable or position sensor may be malfunctioning.␀AMS-HT H communication is abnormal; please check the connection cable.␀AMS-HT H is undergoing dry cooling; please wait for it to cool down before operating.␀AMS-HT H motor was overloaded. The filament may be tangled or the filament buffer may be stuck.␀AMS-HT H heater malfunction or the current sensor is abnormal.␀AMS-HT H The heater is disconnected, which may be due to poor connector contact.␀AMS-HT H heater is short-circuited, which may be due to a wiring short or heater damage.␀AMS-HT H The heater is heating abnormally.␀AMS-HT H The coil resistance of exhaust valve 1 is abnormal, which may be due to abnormal wiring or damage.␀AMS-HT H The exhaust valve 1 is not connected, which may be due to poor connector contact.␀The current sensor of AMS-HT H exhaust valve 1 is abnormal; please get in touch with customer support to replace the AMS-HT mainboard.␀AMS-HT H The operation of the exhaust valve 1 is abnormal, which may be due to excessive resistance.␀AMS-HT H The coil resistance of exhaust valve 2 is abnormal, which may be due to abnormal wiring or damage.␀AMS-HT H The exhaust valve 2 is not connected, which may be due to poor connector contact.␀The current sensor of AMS-HT H exhaust valve 2 is abnormal; please get in touch with customer support to replace the AMS-HT mainboard.␀AMS-HT H The operation of the exhaust valve 2 is abnormal, which may be due to excessive resistance.␀AMS-HT H heater cooling fan is blocked, which may be due to the fan being stuck.␀AMS-HT H The heater cooling fan speed is too low, which could be due to excessive fan resistance.␀AMS-HT H heater cooling fan cannot start because the power adapter is not connected.␀AMS-HT H heater temperature sensor is offline, which may be due to poor connector contact.␀Temperature sensor on the AMS-HT H heater was malfunction, resulting in abnormal temperature readings.␀AMS-HT H The drying process may experience thermal runaway. Please turn off the AMS power supply.␀AMS-HT H Unable to start drying; please pull out the filament from filament hub and try again.␀AMS-HT H Environmental temperature is too low, which will affect the drying capability.␀AMS-HT H The temperature control error is too large, which may be due to the lid being open or an abnormality with the heater.␀AMS-HT H chamber temperature is too high; auxiliary feeding or RFID reading is currently not allowed.␀AMS-HT H The power adapter voltage is too low, which may result in insufficient drying temperature. Please replace the power adapter.␀AMS-HT H The power adapter voltage is too high, which may damage the heater circuit. Please replace the power adapter.␀The RFID-tag on AMS-HT A cannot be identified.␀The RFID-tag on AMS-HT B cannot be identified.␀The RFID-tag on AMS-HT C cannot be identified.␀The RFID-tag on AMS-HT D cannot be identified.␀The RFID-tag on AMS-HT E cannot be identified.␀The RFID-tag on AMS-HT F cannot be identified.␀The RFID-tag on AMS-HT G cannot be identified.␀The RFID-tag on AMS-HT H cannot be identified.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀J␀␀␀∑␀␀␀¸␀␀␀Æ␀␀¯␀␀B␀␀¶␀␀Ô␀␀T␀␀ﬂ␀␀G␀␀ê␀␀Ÿ␀␀␀␀Â␀␀i␀␀≤␀␀F␀␀º␀␀,␀␀®␀␀	␀␀c	␀␀î	␀␀÷	␀␀.
